1. TimescaleDB Community Edition  --  Timescale License (TSL)   [important]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The bundled PostgreSQL images ship the TimescaleDB extension:

    timescale/timescaledb:2.17.2-pg16
        official image, re-pushed as nereidai/timescaledb:2.17.2-pg16
        (standalone / docker-compose path; deploy/images/postgres/Dockerfile)
    nereidai/postgresql:16.4-timescale-tsl
        CloudNativePG image extending the CNPG catalog PostgreSQL 16.4 with
        the TimescaleDB 2.26.4 community .deb from the packagecloud repo
        (deploy/images/postgres/Dockerfile.cnpg)

The PostgreSQL engine itself is under the PostgreSQL License (a permissive
MIT/BSD-style license). The TimescaleDB extension is dual-licensed:

    * TimescaleDB Apache-2 Edition  -> Apache License 2.0 (OSI open source)
    * TimescaleDB Community Edition -> Timescale License (TSL),
      source-available but NOT an OSI-approved open-source license.

The images above are the Community Edition and contain "-tsl" binaries.
NereidLink relies on Community-Edition features:

    * hypertables, create_hypertable(), drop_chunks()
        -- these core functions are also in the Apache-2 edition;
    * continuous aggregates (ts_telemetry_hourly, ts_telemetry_daily),
        refresh_continuous_aggregate(), add_continuous_aggregate_policy()
        -- TSL only (introduced in schema migration 0024);
    * native columnar compression and add_compression_policy()
        -- TSL only (migration 0024);
    * add_retention_policy()
        -- TSL only (migration 0036, accounting_topn).

What TSL permits.  You may run Community Edition free of charge, including
commercially and as part of a hosted service, provided NereidLink is offered
as a VALUE-ADDED product or service: it is an IoT platform, not a hosted
time-series database; users cannot run DDL or otherwise define or modify the
TimescaleDB schema themselves (the schema is managed exclusively by NereidLink
migrations). Private/on-premise redistribution inside the product is allowed.

What TSL prohibits.  You may NOT offer TimescaleDB Community Edition itself
as a hosted/managed database-as-a-service (or otherwise expose its
data-definition/data-manipulation interfaces to third parties as a database
service), and you may not redistribute modified TSL source or binaries. To
offer a managed database service you must use TimescaleDB Apache-2 Edition,
which does not provide continuous aggregates, compression, or retention
policies and therefore cannot run the current schema migrations unchanged.

Redistribution obligations (TSL section 2.1(b)).  When you redistribute the
bundled database image you must: (1) tell recipients it includes TimescaleDB
Community Edition under the Timescale License and provide the license text or
the URL below; (2) keep recipients from defining/modifying the TimescaleDB
schema (NereidLink enforces this technically); and (3) refer to the component
as "TimescaleDB Community Edition" (and "TimescaleDB Apache-2 Edition" for
the Apache build).

License text and details:
    https://www.timescale.com/legal/licenses
    https://github.com/timescale/timescaledb/blob/main/tsl/LICENSE-TIMESCALE

NereidLink only communicates with PostgreSQL over SQL; no TSL code is compiled
or linked into the NereidLink binary, so the NereidLink source remains
Apache-2.0. The TSL-licensed functions are isolated in database migrations
0024/0036 and the rollup/retention paths; the rest of the product does not
depend on them.

